@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:automation] validated-rules-update
The scheduled rules workflow MUST finish its validation and build gates before
committing or pushing an update. Its commits MUST be restricted to the vendored
database, license, and provenance manifest.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:automation] validated-main-push
Automatic rules updates MUST use GITHUB_TOKEN to push normally to main only when
the validated base is still current. The workflow MUST NOT force-push or rebase
onto unvalidated code. A successful update push MUST explicitly dispatch CI.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:testing] hosted-worker-isolation
Hosted integration tests MUST exercise the real Bubblewrap sandbox. Runner setup
MAY permit the pinned Bubblewrap executable to create user namespaces, but MUST
NOT disable host-wide AppArmor restrictions or skip sandboxed attachment tests.
